  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Scaled Dot-Product Attention** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np, math\n\ndef dl_scaled_dot_product_attention(Q: list, K: list, V: list) -> list:\n    q, k, v = np.array(Q, dtype=float), np.array(K, dtype=float), np.array(V, dtype=float)\n    s = (q @ k.T) / math.sqrt(q.shape[-1])\n    e = np.exp(s - np.max(s, axis=-1, keepdims=True))\n    return np.round((e / np.sum(e, axis=-1, keepdims=True)) @ v, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
